@@ -79,6 +79,57 @@
                   </ui-tree>
                 </ui-example>
               </ui-section>
+              <ui-section id="examples-types-columns" label="Columns" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
+                <ui-example description="With `mode=&quot;columns&quot;`, a column per level, as a file browser's column view:  picking a row with rows inside it opens them in the next column.  Up and down select in a column, right goes in, left comes back out.">
+                  <ui-tree mode="columns" label="Files" style="max-width: 48em">
+                    <ui-tree-item label="src" icon="folder">
+                      <ui-tree-item label="Card.spellml" icon="file code"></ui-tree-item>
+                      <ui-tree-item label="Deck.spellml" icon="file code"></ui-tree-item>
+                      <ui-tree-item label="styles" icon="folder">
+                        <ui-tree-item label="card.css" icon="file code" selected></ui-tree-item>
+                      </ui-tree-item>
+                    </ui-tree-item>
+                    <ui-tree-item label="README.md" which="notes" icon="file alternate outline"></ui-tree-item>
+                  </ui-tree>
+                </ui-example>
+              </ui-section>
+              <ui-section id="examples-types-columns-from-data" label="Columns from data" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
+                <ui-example description="A big tree is given as data, in `items`:  each item's `children` a list, or a function run the first time it opens.  Only the open path's columns are drawn.  `counts` shows how many rows each holds;  `filter` filters the last column, here the 300 cells of `alu`.">
+                  <ui-tree id="netlist-columns" mode="columns" counts label="Netlist" style="--ui-tree-column-width: 13em"></ui-tree>
+                  <ui-input id="netlist-filter" icon="search" placeholder="Filter the last column" style="margin-top: 0.5em"></ui-input>
+                  <script type="module">
+                    const kinds = ["nand2", "nor2", "inv", "dff", "mux2", "xor2"]
+                    const cells = (prefix, count) =>
+                      Array.from({ length: count }, (_, at) => {
+                        const kind = kinds[at % kinds.length]
+                        const id = `u_${kind}_${at}`
+                        return {
+                          id,
+                          label: id,
+                          which: kind,
+                          icon: "microchip",
+                          children: ["A", "B", "Y"].map((pin) => ({ id: pin, label: pin, which: `${prefix}/${id}/${pin}`, icon: "circle outline" }))
+                        }
+                      })
+                    const block = (id, sizes) => ({
+                      id,
+                      label: id,
+                      icon: "cube",
+                      children: () => Object.entries(sizes).map(([name, size]) => ({ id: name, label: name, icon: "cubes", count: size, children: () => cells(`${id}/${name}`, size) }))
+                    })
+                    await customElements.whenDefined("ui-tree")
+                    const tree = document.getElementById("netlist-columns")
+                    tree.items = [
+                      block("cpu", { alu: 300, regfile: 64, decoder: 48 }),
+                      block("gpu", { shader: 120, raster: 80 }),
+                      block("mem_ctrl", { phy: 40, sched: 96 }),
+                      block("uart", { tx: 12, rx: 12 })
+                    ]
+                    tree.path = ["cpu", "alu", "u_nand2_6"]
+                    document.getElementById("netlist-filter").addEventListener("input", (event) => (tree.filter = event.target.value))
+                  </script>
+                </ui-example>
+              </ui-section>
             </ui-section>
             <ui-section id="examples-content" label="Content" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
               <ui-section id="examples-content-which-one" label="Which one" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
@@ -130,6 +181,13 @@
                   - `open` shows the rows inside it.  A row whose rows are drawn only once it opens says `expandable`.
                   - `ui-changed` hands over what's selected.  To decide that yourself, cancel `ui-selecting`, and set each row's `selected`.
                   - `filter` looks only at rows that are drawn.
+
+                  `mode="columns"` lays it out as a file browser's column view.
+                  - Its rows can be `<ui-tree-item>`s, or data in the `items` property:  `{ id, label, icon?, which?, count?, children?, data? }`,
+                    where `children` is a list, or a function run the first time the item opens.  Only the open path's columns are drawn.
+                  - `path` is the ids from the top down to the selected item;  set it to open a path.  `ui-changed` hands over `path` and `item`.
+                  - `filter` filters one column:  the last one on screen when the filter starts, until it's cleared.
+                  - `--ui-tree-column-width` sets each column's width, `--ui-tree-columns-height` their height.
                 </script>
               </ui-markdown>
               <ui-code language="js">
@@ -145,6 +203,9 @@
                   - Up and down move between the rows on screen;  Home and End go to the ends.
                   - Right opens a row, then goes into it;  left closes it, then goes out to its parent.
                   - Enter and Space select, with Shift, Command or Control as a click takes them.
+
+                  In columns mode, the keys select as they move:  up and down in a column, Home and End to its ends, right into the
+                  next column, left back out.
                 </script>
               </ui-markdown>
             </ui-section>
